    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "PSA\n727-100\nEMERGENCY EXITS\nThere are seven exits provided for your use. The chart below will\nshow you the one closest to your seat. The exits over the wings\nare removable windows. The two exits forward are doors which\nare equipped with fast operating evacuation slides.\nWINDOW EXITS\nSTEP 1\nSTEP 2\nB\nEMERGENCY EXITS\nFORWARD\nCABIN\nDOOR\nSLIDE\nPULL\nDOWN\nTHIS\nFLAP\nGRASP\nHANDLE\nAND\nPULL\nDOWN\nSERVICE\nDOOR\nSLIDE\nPULL\nTOP\nINWARD\nAND\nLIFT\nCABIN DOORS\nWINDOW\nEXITS\nWINDOW\nEXITS\nROTATE\nHANDLE\nPUSH\nDOOR\nOUT\nTOPEN\nCLOSED\nSLIDE\nMAIN REAR\nCABIN DOOR\nPLACARDS GIVING\nSTEPS FOR OPERATION\nOF\nEVACUATION\nSLIDE\nARE LOCATED ON EACH\nDOOR. SLIDE IS\nSHOWN\nREADY FOR USE.\nSEE REVERSE SIDE\nPLEASE DO NOT REMOVE FROM AIRCRAFT",
      "PSA\n727\nIMPORTANT INFORMATION\nFOR OUR FANJET PASSENGERS\nEven though you may be an experienced air\ntraveler, there are certain features of this air-\ncraft with which you may not be familiar.\nAUTOMATIC OXYGEN SYSTEM\nThe higher altitudes at which this aircraft operates require the\nprompt use of the automatic oxygen system in case of any\nsudden change in cabin pressure. Should a decompression occur\noxygen masks will drop down. Pull nearest mask down to initiate\nflow of oxygen and promptly place over nose and mouth. Adjust\nheadband. Breathe normally.\nNO SMOKING\nBREATHE\nNORMALLY\nFLOTATION EQUIPMENT\nFORWARD\nFACING\nSEAT\nBRACING POSITION\nREAR\nFACING\nSEAT\nIn\nthe\nevent of a water landing,\ncushion\nmay be used as an aid to\nkeep afloat. Grasp the cushion at the\nrear, pull it forward and take it with\nyou. Place arms through straps on\nbottom to retain cushion.\nSEAT BELT\nLIFT TO\nRELEASE\nAT 8-10 10/78\nEven if the \"SEAT BELT\" sign is turned off in flight, it is recommended\nthat you keep your seat belt loosely fastened, whenever you are in your\nseat.\nPLEASE DO NOT REMOVE FROM AIRCRAFT\nSEE REVERSE SIDE\n2-5-5/76 2005.133.337"
    ],
